WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.760
A report is only as strong as the model behind it.

2
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:09.800
In this lesson, you will learn to read Model view, let Power BI find

3
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:16.280
relationships with Autodetect, and then check its work, so every number you show is right. Let's start building!

4
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.706
Welcome to Model view.

5
00:00:19.706 --> 00:00:21.713
Each box is a table:

6
00:00:21.713 --> 00:00:23.319
Customers, Orders, Products, Categories.

7
00:00:23.319 --> 00:00:29.340
Right now they are not connected, so Power BI does not know how they relate.

8
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.428
On the Home tab, open Manage relationships and click Autodetect.

9
00:00:49.428 --> 00:00:56.520
Power BI compares names and data across tables, and finds thirteen relationships for us. Nice!

10
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.615
But remember: Autodetect only guesses.

11
00:01:11.615 --> 00:01:16.595
It matches columns that look alike, like Customer ID in Customers and Orders.

12
00:01:16.595 --> 00:01:20.425
It can miss a link, or create a wrong one.

13
00:01:20.425 --> 00:01:22.340
So always check its work.

14
00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.214
Here is the list.

15
00:01:55.214 --> 00:02:01.269
For each relationship, you see the two tables, the linking columns, and whether it is active.

16
00:02:01.269 --> 00:02:03.540
Running Autodetect again finds nothing new.

17
00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:11.016
Back in Model view, lines now connect the tables.

18
00:02:11.016 --> 00:02:17.280
The marks on each line show the cardinality, like one to many, and the direction filters flow.

19
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.077
Want to start over, or remove a wrong link?

20
00:02:40.077 --> 00:02:43.078
Select it in Manage relationships and click Delete.

21
00:02:43.078 --> 00:02:46.080
Then create the right one with New relationship.

22
00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:03.300
A clean model makes every report faster and every number more reliable. Great work!

